# CUBE CSS Pattern Library

This pattern library documents the design primitives and components available in the **Cube** style, organised according to the [CUBE CSS](https://cube.fyi/) methodology.

## What is CUBE CSS?

CUBE stands for **Composition, Utility, Block, Exception** --- a CSS methodology that embraces the cascade rather than fighting it. Instead of scoping every element, CUBE layers its styles so that each layer has a clear, predictable responsibility:

{.flow}
- **Tokens** --- design decisions expressed as CSS custom properties: colours, spacing scales, type scales, and radii.
- **Resets** --- a thin normalisation layer that levels browser defaults.
- **Globals** --- document-wide typographic and flow rules applied through the cascade.
- **Fonts** --- web-font declarations and font-stack definitions.
- **Compositions** --- skeletal layout primitives (stack, cluster, sidebar, grid, switcher, etc.) that control _how elements relate to each other_ without dictating appearance.
- **Utilities** --- single-purpose classes that apply a single token or property (text sizes, colours, spacing, etc.).
- **Blocks** --- the styled components: buttons, cards, prose regions, tags, and so on. Each block owns its own cosmetic rules.
- **Exceptions** --- context-specific overrides applied via data attributes (e.g., `[data-variant="narrow"]`).

## How Wig works with CUBE CSS

Wig treats CUBE CSS as a first-class citizen. Each style declares its patterns in `patterns/` directories, organised into the categories above. At build time Wig:

{.flow}
1. Discovers pattern files (HTML with YAML front-matter) in each category directory.
2. Auto-bundles the associated CSS into a single stylesheet ordered by `@layer` --- tokens first, exceptions last --- so that the cascade works correctly without manual ordering.
3. Exposes every pattern, its rendered HTML, and its variants in the template context for pagination and display.

Browse the sidebar to explore each pattern. Click any item to see a live preview with viewport controls.
